30,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial significantly reduced readmissions for seniors, but the shared nursing round suffered from high visit failure rates.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Our rooms and parking are at capacity by mid-morning. Furthermore, the booking system ignores any work without a fixed slot.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Joint clinics have failed here due to rota disputes. Also, external data agreements take over a year to finalize.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Ward vacancies are high and agency costs are rising, but the midwifery rota actually has some unusual slack.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The budget is down by a quarter, and off-site contacts bring in no regional funding. On-site work is the only way to earn.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if off-site work earns nothing, the Home Follow-Up Team seems financially risky despite the readmission benefits.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, and the Home Follow-Up Team would likely be ""invisible"" work that the booking system fails to record.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the midwifery slack is interesting. A program there might avoid the staffing crises seen in other wards.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,That's true! But we must be careful not to overload the few nurses we have left in other areas.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,Indeed. We need a program that is financially sustainable and doesn't rely on external signatures or unpaid travel.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The Day Rehabilitation Unit would be on-site, but @Toshio, would the parking and room shortage kill it?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Absolutely. Adding a dedicated unit for outpatient therapy would seize up our remaining space and shuttle capacity.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Chronic Care Coordination sounds logical, but it requires those external data agreements I found to be a nightmare.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"If the midwifery team has capacity, the Perinatal Support Service seems the most humane choice for the staff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"And since it is on-site, it would qualify for the standard outpatient tariffs, helping our diminished budget.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,It seems we are balancing patient outcomes against a very rigid set of operational constraints.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,The constraints are the reality. We cannot build what we cannot house or record.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree. The Perinatal service avoids the ""joint venture"" trap if the midwifery slack is utilized correctly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,It feels like the safest bet for the team's mental health too.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us see the candidates and weigh them with this knowledge.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
